        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(android): command palette title appears off-center",
        "body": "[AI-assisted]\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users opening the Android command palette would see the header title shifted slightly to the right instead of centered on the screen.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe avatar now occupies the same 48 dp header slot as the back control, while the visible avatar remains unchanged at 34 dp. This balances the weighted title without changing the back touch target or avatar size.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe command palette title is visually centered, producing a balanced header while preserving the existing controls and behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAndroid emulator behavior verified with the exact patched APK. The measured title offset changed from `+7 dp` before the patch to `0` after it.\n\n<table>\n<tr>\n<th>Before</th>\n<th>After</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><img width=\"260\" alt=\"Before Proof\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4b0e02b4-e098-446d-bbfe-dfb560371ba5\" /></td>\n<td><img width=\"260\" alt=\"After Proof\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/709fafc0-6953-4b30-8ecd-600e0e0988a6\" /></td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\nBefore video — shows the title shifted to the right:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d477e245-8bf8-435c-9d42-8b537eeeaba0\n\nAfter video — shows the centered title with unchanged controls:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/385bb234-3c4c-4cac-b2fb-28bdfe1dea6c\n\nThe refreshed upstream base currently has a pre-existing native i18n inventory mismatch (`4320` extracted entries versus `4309` locale entries); this patch does not modify those locale artifacts.\n",
